# Input for ci/guarddog/requirements.txt. One line, on purpose: everything
# else in that lock is guarddog's own transitive closure, resolved by the
# compiler and never edited by hand.
#
# Regenerate the pair together, with the same hash-locked uv the relock
# workflow uses (`requirements-relock.lock` pins it; plain `pip-compile` is
# neither pinned nor installed anywhere in this repository, so a command
# naming it would not be reproducible in a clean checkout):
#
#     python -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements-relock.lock
#     uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes --strip-extras \
#       --python-version 3.12 \
#       -o ci/guarddog/requirements.txt ci/guarddog/requirements.in
#
# 3.12 because that is the interpreter .github/workflows/guarddog.yml runs
# the scanner on -- unlike the CI locks, this toolchain is never installed
# on the 3.10 matrix cell, so resolving for 3.10 would pin backports the
# scanner job never uses.
#
# The 3.x floor is not cosmetic -- 2.7.0 and below carry
# GHSA-xg9w-vg3g-6m68, a path traversal in safe_extract() that hands a
# scanned package arbitrary file write on the scanner host.
guarddog==3.2.0
